1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,850
Can you describe it so someone else can build it?

2
00:00:02,930 --> 00:00:08,470
In Science Olympiad's Write It Do It, one partner studies a structure and writes instructions.

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:12,297
The other partner rebuilds it, without ever seeing the original.

4
00:00:12,377 --> 00:00:14,450
No pointing. No peeking. Just words.

5
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:18,157
This is a team event, and the instructions are the whole game.

6
00:00:18,237 --> 00:00:20,808
The closer the match, the higher the score.

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,372
Here's the trap.

8
00:00:22,452 --> 00:00:27,092
The writer looks at the structure, and writes: "Put the red piece over there."

9
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:30,682
The builder has to guess. And builds... this.

10
00:00:30,762 --> 00:00:32,664
Wrong spot. Loose connections.

11
00:00:32,744 --> 00:00:34,990
Vague words build the wrong thing.

12
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:38,234
Now the same structure, with precise words.

13
00:00:38,314 --> 00:00:45,007
"Plug the left end of the three-long red rod into the right-facing opening of the straight connector at C two."

14
00:00:45,087 --> 00:00:48,851
"Plug the right end into a second straight connector at G two."

15
00:00:48,931 --> 00:00:51,413
Every piece named. Every connection exact.

16
00:00:51,493 --> 00:00:53,690
Precise words build the right thing.

17
00:00:54,390 --> 00:00:56,134
Ready to try it yourself?

18
00:00:56,214 --> 00:00:58,322
Watch, learn, practice, build.

19
00:00:58,402 --> 00:01:01,758
Start Lesson One, at Made For My Kids dot com.
